          <!-- Working Principle (2026-09-27) -->
          <div class="mt-14">
            <h2 class="text-[clamp(20px,2.2vw,32px)] font-bold text-gray-900 mb-5 font-barlow-condensed">Working Principle of Static Var Generator (SVG)</h2>
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
              <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-gray-600 mb-2">Inside every CHITEK SVG, the CTs sample the load current while the DSP at the core runs the control algorithm. It separates the reactive component from the active current, tracks how the demand moves cycle by cycle, and works out how much leading or lagging current the network needs at that instant.</p>
              <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-gray-600">The DSP then drives the IGBT bridge through PWM. The inverter injects a compensation current in quadrature with the voltage, so the reactive demand is met locally instead of being drawn from the utility. The CTs read the output current too and return it to the DSP as negative feedback — that closed loop is what keeps the correction stepless and continuous, with no contactor steps and no resonance with the grid.</p>
              <img src="/assets/images/working-principle-svg.webp" alt="Working principle of CHITEK static var generator" class="mt-6 w-full rounded-xl" width="1748" height="900" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQs (2026-09-27) — category-level Q&A, deliberately non-overlapping with the AHF category page -->
          <div id="faq" class="mt-14">
            <h2 class="text-[clamp(20px,2.2vw,32px)] font-bold text-gray-900 mb-5 font-barlow-condensed">FAQs About the Static Var Generator (SVG) Series</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
              <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-5" open>
                <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900 text-[clamp(15px,1.35vw,20px)]">Q1: What is the difference between an SVG and a capacitor bank?</summary>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,16px)] leading-relaxed">A static var generator (SVG) is an active, stepless compensator &mdash; it reads the reactive demand continuously and injects exactly what the network needs, so correction tracks the load in real time. A capacitor or reactor bank switches in fixed steps, which means jumps in power factor, possible resonance and regular maintenance. The table below contrasts the two across the dimensions that matter in the field.</p>
<div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white">
  <table class="w-full min-w-[760px] border-collapse text-[clamp(13px,1vw,15px)] leading-relaxed text-left">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <th scope="col" class="w-[16%] bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900"><span class="sr-only">Aspect</span></th>
        <th scope="col" class="w-[42%] bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Capacitor Banks or Reactor Banks</th>
        <th scope="col" class="w-[42%] bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Static Var Generators</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Response time</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Contact-based solutions take at least 30 s to 40 s to mitigate the problem and thyristor-based solutions 20 ms to 30 ms</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Real-time mitigation of power quality problems as the overall response time is less than 100 &mu;s</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Output</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Depends on step sizes; cannot match load demand in real time</li>
          <li>Depends on grid voltage as capacitor units and reactors are used</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Instantaneous, continuous, stepless and seamless</li>
          <li>Grid voltage fluctuation has no influence on the output</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Power factor correction</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Capacitor banks needed for inductive loads and reactor banks for capacitive loads; problems in systems with mixed loads</li>
          <li>Not possible to guarantee unity power factor as they have steps; the system will be having continuous over- and under-compensation</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Corrects simultaneously from &minus;1 to +1 power factor of lagging (inductive) and leading (capacitive) loads</li>
          <li>Guaranteed unity power factor at all times without any over- or under-compensation (stepless output)</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Design &amp; sizing</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Reactive power studies needed to size the proper solution</li>
          <li>Usually oversized to better adjust to changing load demands</li>
          <li>Need to be designed taking into account system harmonics</li>
          <li>Custom-built for specific load and network conditions</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>No extensive studies required as it is adjustable</li>
          <li>Mitigation capacity can be exactly what load demands</li>
          <li>Unaffected by harmonic distortion in the system</li>
          <li>Can adapt to load and network conditions and changes</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Resonance</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Parallel or series resonance can amplify currents in the system</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>No risk of harmonic resonance with the network</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Overloading</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Possible due to slow response and/or variation of loads</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Not possible as current is limited to the max. RMS current</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Footprint &amp; installation</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Medium to large footprint, especially if several harmonic orders</li>
          <li>Not simple installation, especially if loads upgraded frequently</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Small footprint and simple installation as modules are compact in size; existing switchgear can be used</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Expansion</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Limited and depends on load conditions and network topology</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Simple (and not dependent) by adding modules</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 align-top">
        <th scope="row" class="bg-gray-50 py-3 px-4 text-left font-semibold text-gray-900">Maintenance &amp; lifetime</th>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Uses components that need extensive maintenance like fuses, circuit breakers, contactors, reactors and capacitor units</li>
          <li>Switching, transients and resonance reduce lifetime</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
        <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Simple maintenance and service life of up to 15 years as there is no electro-mechanical switching and no risk of transients or resonance</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
              </details>
              <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-5">
                <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900 text-[clamp(15px,1.35vw,20px)]">Q2: Can one SVG follow a fluctuating load?</summary>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,16px)] leading-relaxed">Yes, and that is where it beats a switched bank. Welding, motor starts and drive ramps change the reactive demand many times a second. The generator tracks those changes cycle by cycle, so it also covers the fast swings a contactor-based bank never sees.</p>
              </details>
              <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-5">
                <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900 text-[clamp(15px,1.35vw,20px)]">Q3: Can SVG units be combined for a higher capacity?</summary>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,16px)] leading-relaxed">Yes. The range is modular, so units can be paralleled to cover anything from a single wall-mounted module to a large plant, instead of forcing everything through one oversized cabinet.</p>
              </details>
              <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-5">
                <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-900 text-[clamp(15px,1.35vw,20px)]">Q4: Can SVG be installed outdoors or in harsh environments?</summary>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 text-[clamp(13px,1.15vw,16px)] leading-relaxed">Yes. Alongside indoor enclosures, the range includes IP65 models for outdoor and dusty sites, plus anti-pollution and fanless low-noise versions for switchrooms where dust, corrosion or acoustic noise is the constraint.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <style is:global>
      .cbp-vm-options { display: flex; gap: .5rem; }
      .cbp-vm-icon {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
        /* button 标签必须显式压掉 UA 默认样式，否则宽度/盒模型/字体会顶掉 38×38 布局 */
        width: 38px; min-width: 38px; height: 38px; padding: 0;
        appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
        box-sizing: border-box; flex-shrink: 0;
        font-family: inherit; line-height: 1;
        border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px;
        background: #fff; color: #6b7280; cursor: pointer; transition: all .2s;
        font-size: 18px;
      }
      /* 键盘可达性：原 a[href="#"] 自带焦点环，button 默认会吃色 → 显式补回 */
      .cbp-vm-icon:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #f97316; outline-offset: 2px; }
      .cbp-vm-icon:hover { border-color: #fb923c; color: #ea580c; }
      .cbp-vm-icon.cbp-vm-selected { background: #fff7ed; border-color: #f97316; color: #ea580c; }

      /* Series quick-switch (2026-09-24) — same 38px height as the grid/list icons */
      .cbp-vm-tab {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
        height: 38px; padding: 0 14px; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px;
        background: #fff; color: #4b5563; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; transition: all .2s;
      }
      .cbp-vm-tab:hover { border-color: #fb923c; color: #ea580c; background: #fff7ed; }
      .cbp-vm-tab.cbp-vm-tab-active { background: #fff7ed; border-color: #f97316; color: #ea580c; }

      .cbp-vm-grid-ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
      /* Row gap tightened 40px -> 24px (2026-09-28); column gap kept at 2.5rem */
      .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-grid-ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(1, minmax(0, 1fr)); row-gap: 1.5rem; column-gap: 2.5rem; }
      @media (min-width: 640px)  { .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-grid-ul { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
      @media (min-width: 768px)  { .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-grid-ul { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
      @media (min-width: 1024px) { .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-grid-ul { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }

      /* Grid view: title + brief description only — hide tags and View More (shown in list view) */
      .cbp-vm-view-grid .tags_ul,
      .cbp-vm-view-grid .my_more1,
      .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-actions { display: none; }

      /* Gap between the view-toggle box and the product cards (2026-09-28) */
      #cbp-vm.cbp-vm-switcher { margin-top: 1.5rem; }

      .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-grid-ul { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }

      .cbp-vm-li {
        background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: .75rem;
        overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
        transition: box-shadow .3s, transform .3s;
      }
      .cbp-vm-li:hover { box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,.10); }

      .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-li { flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; }

      .cbp-vm-image { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; background: #f3f4f6; overflow: hidden; }
      /* Grid view: 图框改正方形（宽度占满卡宽，高度跟随宽度 → 1:1） */
      .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-image { aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; }
      .cbp-vm-image img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
      .cbp-vm-image a { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
      .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-image { width: 240px; height: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; aspect-ratio: auto; align-self: center; margin: 1rem 0; }

      .cbp-vm-li .text { padding: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1; }
      .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-li .text { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
      .cbp-vm-li .h4 { font-size: clamp(15px, 1.1vw, 18px); font-weight: 600; color: #111827; margin-bottom: .5rem; line-height: 1.3; }
      .cbp-vm-li .h4 a { text-decoration: none; }
      /* Current-rating suffix (2026-10-12): phone only; 4ch gap matches en/index.astro */
      .cbp-spec { display: none; }
      .cbp-vm-details { font-size: 13px; color: #4b5563; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: .75rem; flex: 1; }
      .tags_ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .375rem; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
      .cbp-tag {
        font-size: 11px; color: #6b7280; background: #f3f4f6;
        border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 8px;
        text-decoration: none; transition: all .2s;
      }
      .cbp-tag:hover { background: #fff7ed; color: #ea580c; border-color: #fdba74; }
      .my_more1 {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; align-self: flex-start;
        font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; text-decoration: none;
        background: #EA511E; border: none; border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 22px;
        transition: background .2s;
      }
      .my_more1:hover { background: #C43B13; }
      /* Download button (2026-09-28) — a real control in the same group as the List view icon:
         it shares .cbp-vm-icon (reset + hover + .cbp-vm-selected highlight) and only widens for text.
         margin-left: -.5rem cancels the parent gap so it sits flush against the list icon. */
      .cbp-vm-dl-hint {
        width: auto; min-width: 0; padding: 0 14px; margin-left: -.5rem;
        font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;
      }

      /* List-view action row: View More + Datasheet / Catalog / Device Manual */
      .cbp-vm-actions {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
        margin-top: auto;
      }
      .cbp-vm-dl { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; }
      /* Wrap instead of forcing the card wider (2026-10-12): without this the
         3-button group's inline-flex min-content width pinned the text column at
         374px and pushed Device Manual 19px outside the card at 640px. */
      .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-dl { flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .cbp-dl-btn {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
        font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #ea580c; text-decoration: none;
        background: #fff7ed; border: 1px solid #fdba74; border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 7px 14px; white-space: nowrap; transition: all .2s;
      }
      .cbp-dl-btn:hover { background: #EA511E; border-color: #EA511E; color: #fff; }
      /* Device Manual 暂无文件：灰色占位（不可点 / 不可聚焦） */
      .cbp-dl-btn.is-off {
        color: #9ca3af; background: #f9fafb; border-color: #e5e7eb;
        cursor: default; pointer-events: none;
      }

      /* Mobile list view (2026-10-12).
         Measured at 390px before this block: the fixed 240x150 thumb left the text
         column 374px wide inside a 347px card (267px overflow) and pushed the
         Datasheet / Catalog / Device Manual buttons 248px past the right edge,
         where overflow:hidden cut them off. Below 640px: shrink the thumb, tighten
         padding, and let all four action buttons flow as one wrapping row
         (.cbp-vm-dl -> display:contents so its buttons join the parent flex row). */
      @media (max-width: 639px) {
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-image {
          width: 104px; height: 104px; margin: .75rem 0 .75rem .75rem;
          align-self: flex-start; border-radius: .5rem;
        }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-li .text { padding: .75rem; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-li .h4 { font-size: 15px; margin-bottom: .375rem; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .tags_ul { gap: .25rem; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-tag { font-size: 10px; padding: 1px 6px; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-actions { gap: .375rem; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-vm-dl { display: contents; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .my_more1 { font-size: 13px; padding: 7px 12px; }
        .cbp-vm-view-list .cbp-dl-btn { font-size: 12px; padding: 6px 10px; }

        /* Phone grid: flatter image band (345x345 -> 345x259).
           object-fit: contain, not cover — measured product bbox spans 7%~94% of the
           image height (distributed-ahf), so any crop cuts the chassis. #fefefe is the
           measured plate colour of every card webp (254,254,254) => seamless. */
        .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-image { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; background: #fefefe; }
        .cbp-vm-view-grid .cbp-vm-image img { object-fit: contain; }
        .cbp-vm-li .h4 .cbp-spec { display: inline; margin-left: 4ch; white-space: nowrap; }
      }

      /* Filter card: checkbox styling */
      .filter_card input[type="checkbox"] {
        width: 16px; height: 16px; accent-color: #EA511E; cursor: pointer; flex-shrink: 0;
      }
    </style>

    <script>
      (function () {
        var container = document.getElementById('cbp-vm');
        if (!container) return;
        var opts = container.parentNode.querySelectorAll('.cbp-vm-options > .cbp-vm-icon');
        opts.forEach(function (el) {
          el.addEventListener('click', function (ev) {
            var view = el.getAttribute('data-view');
            container.classList.remove('cbp-vm-view-grid', 'cbp-vm-view-list');
            container.classList.add(view);
            // Highlight every control bound to the same view, so the icon and the
            // "Download" button light up together (2026-09-28)
            opts.forEach(function (o) {
              o.classList.toggle('cbp-vm-selected', o.getAttribute('data-view') === view);
            });
          });
        });
      })();

      // ----- Filter products by technology / voltage / current / IP / dimensions -----
      (function () {
        var boxes = document.querySelectorAll('.filter_card input[type="checkbox"]');
        var cards = document.querySelectorAll('#cbp-vm .cbp-vm-li');
        var summary = document.querySelector('[data-inquiry-summary]');
        if (!boxes.length || !cards.length) return;
        var labels = { t: 'Technology', v: 'Voltage', a: 'Current', i: 'IP Rating', s: 'Dimensions' };
        function apply() {
          var active = { t: [], v: [], a: [], i: [], s: [] };
          boxes.forEach(function (cb) {
            if (cb.checked) {
              var g = cb.getAttribute('data-filter');
              if (active[g]) cb.value.split('|').forEach(function (x) { active[g].push(x); });
            }
          });
          cards.forEach(function (card) {
            var show = true;
            ['t', 'v', 'a', 'i', 's'].forEach(function (g) {
              if (active[g].length) {
                var vals = (card.getAttribute('data-' + g) || '').split(',');
                if (!active[g].some(function (x) { return vals.indexOf(x) > -1; })) show = false;
              }
            });
            card.style.display = show ? '' : 'none';
          });
          if (summary) {
            var lines = [];
            ['t', 'v', 'a', 'i', 's'].forEach(function (g) {
              if (active[g].length) lines.push(labels[g] + ': ' + active[g].join(', '));
            });
            summary.value = lines.join('\n');
          // ---- 选项后的 (N)：命中该选项的型号数（本组按 OR 不算自己，其它组按已勾选过滤）----
          var GROUPS = ['t', 'v', 'a', 'i', 's'];
          function matchOthers(card, skipGroup) {
            for (var i = 0; i < GROUPS.length; i++) {
              var g2 = GROUPS[i];
              if (g2 === skipGroup || !active[g2].length) continue;
              var vals2 = (card.getAttribute('data-' + g2) || '').split(',');
              var hit2 = false;
              for (var j = 0; j < active[g2].length; j++) {
                if (vals2.indexOf(active[g2][j]) > -1) { hit2 = true; break; }
              }
              if (!hit2) return false;
            }
            return true;
          }
          boxes.forEach(function (cb) {
            var g = cb.getAttribute('data-filter');
            var mine = cb.value.split('|');
            var n = 0;
            cards.forEach(function (card) {
              if (!matchOthers(card, g)) return;
              var vals = (card.getAttribute('data-' + g) || '').split(',');
              for (var k = 0; k < mine.length; k++) {
                if (vals.indexOf(mine[k]) > -1) { n++; return; }
              }
            });
            var out = cb.parentNode.querySelector('[data-count]');
            if (out) out.textContent = '(' + n + ')';
          });
          }
        }
        boxes.forEach(function (cb) { cb.addEventListener('change', apply); });
        apply();
      })();

      // Inquire Now (filter): carry the live selection summary into the contact form's Project Requirements
      (function () {
        var btn = document.getElementById('inquire-now-btn');
        if (!btn) return;
        btn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
          var summary = document.querySelector('[data-inquiry-summary]');
          var val = summary ? (summary.value || '').trim() : '';
          if (!val) return; // nothing selected -> navigate to contact normally
          e.preventDefault();
          var base = btn.getAttribute('href') || '/contact';
          var sep = base.indexOf('?') > -1 ? '&' : '?';
          window.location.href = base + sep + 'inquiry=' + encodeURIComponent(val);
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
